  "engineering": {
    "durationMs": 172052.3469,
    "chapters": [
      {
        "start": 448.66990000000806,
        "text": "The architecture is one API, one worker, and PostgreSQL. Signed HTTP acceptance commits first; asynchronous processing has its own durable history."
      },
      {
        "start": 18465.818400000004,
        "text": "Identity is source plus event ID. HMAC covers the exact timestamp and request bytes. Changed bytes under an existing identity are rejected rather than replacing history."
      },
      {
        "start": 36474.91650000001,
        "text": "A transaction combines the refund projection, processing receipt, completion ledger, attempt outcome, and inbox outcome. The guarantee covers these database-local effects."
      },
      {
        "start": 52867.66940000001,
        "text": "Now the normal worker is stopped. Owned test workers will be killed at real commit boundaries. These demonstrations use two-second leases; normal leases are thirty seconds."
      },
      {
        "start": 62347.081000000006,
        "text": "Before commit: no projection, processing receipt, or completion has committed. Killing the actual worker PID 7324 now."
      },
      {
        "start": 65706.31280000001,
        "text": "After commit: the processing receipt and one completion already exist. Killing the actual worker PID 24632 now."
      },
      {
        "start": 71428.3406,
        "text": "Before-commit termination rolled back all local effects. After lease expiry, recovery recorded an abandoned attempt and a successful second attempt, with one completion."
      },
      {
        "start": 98630.9007,
        "text": "After-commit termination preserved the completed transaction. A replacement worker processed a fresh probe, while this original event kept one attempt and one completion."
      },
      {
        "start": 122831.1856,
        "text": "The old owner paused after claiming. A replacement acquired the expired lease and committed. Resuming the old owner produced lost_lease and changed no committed outcome."
      },
      {
        "start": 144920.6283,
        "text": "The proof includes actual worker PIDs, barrier observations, database snapshots, and process logs. Run pnpm verify to repeat it; disposable services and secrets are removed afterward."
      },
      {
        "start": 159936.6967,
        "text": "Scope: synthetic events and one local database. External payments or network calls need their own idempotency protocol. This finite lab retains deduplication identities without expiry."
      }
    ]
  },
